WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.799 --> 00:00:03.179
And now for something completely nuts.

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:08.029
Birds of Prey (And the Fantabulous Emancipation
of One Harley Quinn) has had its early preview

00:00:08.029 --> 00:00:11.500
screenings, and audiences have taken to the
internet to voice their opinions.

00:00:11.500 --> 00:00:16.030
The general consensus: the flick is a raunchy,
funny, very gory good time.

00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:20.400
In case you've missed Birds of Prey's totally
bonkers trailer, the movie follows Margot

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:24.890
Robbie's Harley Quinn following her breakup
with Jared Leto's Joker from Suicide Squad,

00:00:24.890 --> 00:00:27.039
who doesn't make an appearance in this film.

00:00:27.039 --> 00:00:31.689
She's sucked into some nefarious plot involving
the notorious gangster Black Mask, played

00:00:31.689 --> 00:00:36.910
by Ewan McGregor, and must eventually enlist
fellow badasses Black Canary and Huntress

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:39.109
to help protect young Cassandra Cain.

00:00:39.109 --> 00:00:42.859
Robbie's Harley was one of Suicide Squad's
few bright spots, and audiences have been

00:00:42.859 --> 00:00:45.040
anxiously awaiting her return to the role.

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:50.109
Birds of Prey is largely Harley's show and
those preview audiences haven't seen a goofy,

00:00:50.109 --> 00:00:54.749
mayhem-driven comic book character so thoroughly
inhabited by an actor since the last Deadpool

00:00:54.749 --> 00:00:55.749
movie.

00:00:55.749 --> 00:00:56.920
Let's dig into what they had to say.

00:00:56.920 --> 00:00:59.829
First things first: this isn't a comic book
film that you'll want to bring the kiddies

00:00:59.829 --> 00:01:00.829
along for.

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:05.260
Birds of Prey is a hard-R, with copious amounts
of rough language and the kind of violence

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:07.830
usually reserved for Saw movies and the like.

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:12.520
One Reddit user posted a lengthy review of
the film in which he broke down just how inappropriate

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:15.090
Birds of Prey really is for the youngsters,
writing,

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:19.440
"This might be the goriest mainstream comic
book movie I've ever seen...There's a lot

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:20.560
of cursing, as well.

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:22.850
This is a movie that is really not met for
children.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:23.850
It's pretty brutal.

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:25.220
I think teens will love this, though.

00:01:25.220 --> 00:01:27.070
I think this will make John Wick numbers."

00:01:27.070 --> 00:01:31.650
As far as just how enjoyable all of this mayhem
was, the Redditor was duly impressed, adding,

00:01:31.650 --> 00:01:33.590
"It's way better than Suicide Squad.

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:36.740
The jokes are funnier...I thought Ewan McGregor
stole the show.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:40.130
The actress who played Cassandra Cain was
also surprisingly good."

00:01:40.130 --> 00:01:44.480
Over on Letterboxd, one user was enthralled
to see a group of kick-ass women, writing,

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.430
"The film doesn't make much sense.

00:01:46.430 --> 00:01:50.280
But all my life I've seen films about guys
fighting without any reason.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:54.190
And now, watching girls kicking some asses
for any reason, fills you with power.

00:01:54.190 --> 00:01:55.890
[Is] this is what empowerment feels like?

00:01:55.890 --> 00:01:58.820
Is this what boys feel when watching those
nonsense films?

00:01:58.820 --> 00:01:59.960
GIVE ME MORE!"

00:01:59.960 --> 00:02:04.780
Generally, the response to the film so far
is positive, with the vast majority of preview

00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:09.030
audience members claiming that it's far superior
to Suicide Squad, which isn’t very hard

00:02:09.030 --> 00:02:13.500
to do, and even belongs with the likes of
Wonder Woman and Shazam! among the best flicks

00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:15.740
in the interconnected DC Extended Universe.

00:02:15.740 --> 00:02:20.350
It's worth noting that these audience members
tended to exclude Joker from the discussions,

00:02:20.350 --> 00:02:24.300
as it's understood to be completely separate
from the rest of DC's offerings.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:26.100
Another Letterboxd user wrote,

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:30.720
"Margot Robbie is amazing as Harley Quinn,
and [Cassandra Cain] steals all the scenes...Ewan

00:02:30.720 --> 00:02:35.280
as Black Mask is fantastic, the character
is sadistic and cruel, and he managed to convey

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:39.070
all the essence of the villain...It's a good
film, one of the best in DC."

00:02:39.070 --> 00:02:40.070
"Hoo!

00:02:40.070 --> 00:02:43.080
Who's having a good time?"

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.960
Another viewer concurred, while pointing out
that the flick is more than just a re-skin

00:02:46.960 --> 00:02:49.250
of Marvel's popular R-rated franchise.

00:02:49.250 --> 00:02:50.250
The user explained,

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:54.670
"Despite a confusing edit in the first act
and a slightly flat villain, [Birds of Prey]

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:57.260
delivers a fresh take on the superhero movies
field.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:03:01.740
[It] should not be reduced to the 'female
Deadpool' as this one has more charm, a stronger

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:05.480
cast and is still interconnected to the [DC
Extended Universe]."

00:03:05.480 --> 00:03:09.650
Finally, one particular audience member on
Letterboxd weighed in with an opinion that

00:03:09.650 --> 00:03:13.380
we're not sure we can get behind, although
it is eloquent in its brevity.

00:03:13.380 --> 00:03:14.530
They said simply,

00:03:14.530 --> 00:03:15.740
"MCU IS DEAD."

00:03:15.740 --> 00:03:19.790
Somehow, we doubt that Harley and pals will
be putting the final nail in the coffin of

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:24.220
that franchise but if there's any doubt that
the DCEU's course-correction after the stunning

00:03:24.220 --> 00:03:28.349
failure of Justice League is in full swing,
Birds of Prey should put it to rest.

00:03:28.349 --> 00:03:32.420
The flick opens wide on February 7th, 2020.

